# Linting, formatting & types — must pass before "done"

Run and pass every command below **locally before considering a change complete / before committing** (no CI — this discipline is the only gate). Auto-fix first, then fix what remains — never disable a rule to make it pass without justification.

## Definition of done (any code change)
- **Backend:** `ruff check .` clean · `ruff format --check .` clean · `mypy` clean · `pytest -m "unit or integration"` green.
- **Frontend:** `npm run lint` clean · `npm run format` applied · `npm run build` (`tsc -b && vite build`) typechecks · `npm run test` green.

## Backend — ruff + mypy (Python 3.12, `uv`)
Commands (`cd backend`):
```bash
uv run ruff check . --fix && uv run ruff format .      # auto-fix + format
uv run ruff check . && uv run ruff format --check .    # verify
uv run mypy .
```
`pyproject.toml` config (canonical — keep in sync):
```toml
[tool.ruff]
target-version = "py312"
line-length = 99
src = ["app"]

[tool.ruff.lint]
select = ["E","W","F","I","UP","B","SIM","N","RUF","S","C4","PT","ERA","T20","DTZ","PIE","RET","PLR","C901","ASYNC"]
ignore = ["E501","RET504","B008"]   # E501=formatter; B008=FastAPI Depends()

[tool.ruff.lint.per-file-ignores]
"**/tests/**" = ["S101","S105","S106","PLR2004"]   # asserts/magic values OK in tests
"backend/migrations/**" = ["ERA","E402","S608"]     # Alembic templates

[tool.ruff.lint.mccabe]
max-complexity = 10
[tool.ruff.lint.pylint]
max-statements = 20
max-branches = 6
max-returns = 4
max-args = 6
[tool.ruff.format]
quote-style = "double"
indent-style = "space"
line-ending = "lf"

[tool.mypy]
python_version = "3.12"
strict = true
plugins = ["pydantic.mypy"]
warn_unused_ignores = true
disallow_untyped_defs = true
```
- `# type: ignore[code]` / `# noqa: RULE` only with a specific code **and** a short reason comment. No blanket `# type: ignore`.

## Frontend — ESLint + Prettier + tsc (strict TS)
- **Strict TypeScript**, no `any`. Prettier is the single source of formatting truth.
- ESLint enforces the size limits from rule `70-frontend`: **`max-lines` 110** (component/file), **`max-lines-per-function` 60**, **`max-depth` 3**. Barrels (`index.ts`) and test files relax `max-lines`/`max-lines-per-function`.
- `.prettierrc`: `{ semi:false, singleQuote:true, trailingComma:"all", printWidth:90, tabWidth:2, arrowParens:"always", endOfLine:"lf" }`.
- `eslint.config.js` includes `prettier/prettier: 'error'` (via `eslint-plugin-prettier` + `eslint-config-prettier`) so format violations fail lint.

Do not commit code that fails these checks. If a rule genuinely doesn't fit, discuss it and scope the exception in config (per-file-ignores), not with scattered inline disables.
